adius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is  \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(7,3)$ and $Y(-1,3),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{{(7-(-1))}^{2}+{(3-3)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{8}{2}=4.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{7+(-1)}{2},\\frac{3+3}{2})=(3,3)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=4$ and center $(a,b)=(3,3),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ (x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2} & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534047 true] [17592186275958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275959 13194139534047 true] [17592186275958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275960 13194139534047 true] [17592186275958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275961 13194139534047 true] [17592186275958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275962 13194139534047 true] [17592186275958 1000 #edb/ref 17592186275963 13194139534047 true] [17592186275958 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534047 true] [17592186275958 1041 "selection" 13194139534047 true] [17592186275958 1104 #edb/ref 17592186275961 13194139534047 true] [17592186275958 1110 #uuid "82e6df64-4fae-5569-8df0-d3b7494b52b6" 13194139534047 true] [17592186275959 1034 "(x+3)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=4" 13194139534047 true] [17592186275959 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534047 true] [17592186275959 1111 #uuid "4c6b5918-df87-5e8e-aaae-c22b4e7a1fce" 13194139534047 true] [17592186275960 1034 "(x-3)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=4" 13194139534047 true] [17592186275960 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534047 true] [17592186275960 1111 #uuid "78e9081e-db8a-55e5-8820-0a5e81399707" 13194139534047 true] [175921862